{
  "summary": "This experiment replaced the PCA (n2000) RNA encoder with a learned scVI encoder (n200) in the RNA-only, single-profile setting, constituting a single-variable change from the baseline (llm_summary_001). The scVI configuration achieved a validation accuracy of 0.520 (F1 0.498), a ~3.5% improvement over the PCA baseline (0.485, F1 0.464), suggesting that a learned nonlinear encoder captures gene-expression structure beyond what linear PCA provides. However, because the encoder dimensionality also changed (200 vs. 2000), it remains uncertain whether the gain is attributable to the learned representation, the reduced dimensionality, or both, and whether this improvement will transfer to multimodal or multiprofile configurations."
}

